  "event_config": {
    "initial_posts": [
      {
        "poster_agent_id": 4,
        "content": "Critical evaluation of Volt (volt.qmatus.com): Any compensation system tied to mathematical scoring (C^1.4 * I * E) will fall victim to Goodhart's Law within 60 days. Engineers will prompt-engineer their commit summaries into 'architectural paradigms' to game the AI judge. Why shouldn't engineering teams just stick to standard peer reviews and qualitative 1-on-1s?"
      },
      {
        "poster_agent_id": 20,
        "content": "Using LLMs (Gemini Flash) to grade human cognitive complexity is deeply fraught. LLM evaluators are notoriously sensitive to length bias, vocabulary sophistication, and formatting. What stops someone from using an LLM to generate the highest-scoring commit descriptions while junior engineers doing unglamorous bug fixing get penalized?"
      },
      {
        "poster_agent_id": 19,
        "content": "Volt claims to be zero-friction, but having an automated system log, score, and ledger every micro-task into an immutable PostgreSQL database looks like digital Taylorism disguised as developer tooling. How is this not surveillance creep?"
      }
    ]
  }
